## Environments

This project uses environment variables for all secrets and configuration.
**No secrets should ever be hardcoded in source files.**

### Local Development

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your values
2. Source it before running commands: `source .env` (bash) or `set -a; source .env; set +a`
3. For multiple environments, use `.env.dev`, `.env.prod`, etc.

### CI/CD (GitHub Actions)

Secrets and config are managed via **GitHub Environments**:

| Environment | Branch | When |
|---|---|---|
| `dev` | `dev` | Auto-deploy on push |
| `prod` | `main` | Auto-deploy on push (with approval) |

#### Required GitHub Secrets (per environment)

| Secret | Description |
|---|---|
{%- if use_databricks %}
| `DATABRICKS_HOST` | Workspace URL (e.g. `https://adb-XXXX.XX.azuredatabricks.net`) |
| `DATABRICKS_TOKEN` | Personal access token or service principal token |
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_terraform %}
| `ARM_CLIENT_ID` | Azure service principal client ID |
| `ARM_CLIENT_SECRET` | Azure service principal secret |
| `ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` | Azure subscription ID |
| `ARM_TENANT_ID` | Azure AD tenant ID |
{%- endif %}

#### Setting Up GitHub Environments

```bash
# Using gh CLI (recommended)
# 1. Create environments
gh api repos/{{ github_username }}/REPO_NAME/environments/dev -X PUT
gh api repos/{{ github_username }}/REPO_NAME/environments/prod -X PUT

# 2. Add secrets to each environment
gh secret set DATABRICKS_HOST --env dev
gh secret set DATABRICKS_TOKEN --env dev
# ... repeat for prod with prod values

# 3. (Optional) Add protection rules to prod
# Go to: Settings > Environments > prod > Required reviewers
```
{%- if use_dbt %}

### dbt

dbt targets map to environments. Switch with `--target`:

```bash
# Dev (default)
uv run --group dbt dbt build --project-dir dbt/

# Prod
uv run --group dbt dbt build --project-dir dbt/ --target prod
```

Environment variables (`DATABRICKS_HOST`, `DATABRICKS_TOKEN`, `DATABRICKS_HTTP_PATH`) must be set before running dbt.
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_terraform %}

### Terraform

Each environment has its own backend config and variable overrides:

```bash
cd terraform/

# Dev
terraform init -backend-config=environments/dev.backend.hcl
terraform plan -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars

# Prod
terraform init -backend-config=environments/prod.backend.hcl -reconfigure
terraform plan -var-file=environments/prod.tfvars
```

Auth is via `ARM_*` env vars — set them in `.env` or export them directly.
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_databricks %}

### Databricks

Asset Bundle targets map to environments:

```bash
# Dev (default)
databricks bundle deploy -t dev

# Prod
databricks bundle deploy -t prod
```
{%- endif %}

